course: dictionary
lesson: 1670
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one to use. Choke can mean something stuck in your throat, but it can also mean a strong feeling stopping your voice.
explain: «The Mock Turtle, choking with sobs, sings a sad song.» Sobs are crying, so here choking means crying so hard that your voice stops working. Read the words around the word and ask which meaning fits.
explain: «The small birds choke and have to be patted on the back.» The food is stuck, so choke means cannot breathe properly. Test your meaning by putting it in the sentence. Does it still make sense? Yes, it does.
explain: In sport, choke means to fail at an important moment because of nerves. Try the meaning in the sentence and see if it fits the situation.
fact: Choke means to be unable to breathe because something is stuck in your throat.
fact: Choke can also mean to have trouble breathing because of smoke or dust.
fact: Choke up means to have trouble speaking because of strong feelings.
fact: A «choking hazard» is a small object that could make a young child choke.
fact: If someone is choking and cannot cough, speak or breathe, get an adult and call the emergency number.
exercise: «Eating the comfits is noisy: the small birds choke and have to be patted on the back.» What does choke mean here? | *Have food stuck so they cannot breathe well | Shake their wings | Make a loud noise while they sing | Fly away quickly
exercise: «The Mock Turtle, choking with sobs, sings a sad song.» What is the Mock Turtle doing? | Dancing in the sea | Eating soup | Running away from the Queen | *Crying so hard that its voice stops working
exercise: Read a toy's label: «3 and up» means the toy may have small parts. Why is that a choking hazard for a toddler? | The toy is too big to carry | *A small part could get stuck in the toddler's throat | The toy will not make a sound | The toy is too expensive
test: «A toy marked "3 and up" should not be given to a toddler, because it may have small parts that choke.» What is the warning about? | Toys are too expensive for toddlers | Toys are too heavy to lift | Toddlers do not like toys | *Small parts could make a toddler choke
test: «Ava had the winning penalty, but she choked and missed it.» What does choked mean here? | Shouted for joy | Ate a snack before the game | *Failed at an important moment because of nerves | Ran off the pitch in tears
exam: Which sentence uses choke up to mean have trouble speaking because of strong feelings? | Grace ran up the stairs to the library | *Grace choked up as she thanked her friends for the card | Grace ate a grape and sat down | Grace added the numbers quickly
